  "body": "First release.\n\nFills the Nuclear home screen from SoundCloud. Works anonymously out of the box; point it at your profile, or paste an `oauth_token`, and the dashboard is built from your own account.\n\n**Sections**\n\n| Capability | Global | Personal |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Top tracks | trending chart, falling back to featured tracks | your likes, uploads, reposts, listening feed or play history |\n| Top artists | chart authors ranked by charting tracks | who you follow, topped up with the artists you actually listen to |\n| Playlists | editorial selections | your personalised recommendations, or your own and liked playlists |\n\n**Notes**\n\n- No API credentials needed. The `client_id` is scraped from SoundCloud's public bundles and refreshed on 401/403.\n- The optional token is only ever sent to `api-v2.soundcloud.com`, never to the CDN, and a rejected token drops the session back to anonymous rather than blanking the dashboard.\n- `\"Artist - Title\"` is split out of SoundCloud track titles, so the Artist column shows the performer instead of whoever uploaded the file.\n- Recommended playlists open through a dedicated playlists provider that addresses them by URN.\n\nInstall as a dev plugin: `Preferences -> Plugins -> Installed -> Add Plugin`. No build step required."
